<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    THE EIGHTH DAY - spawning.xml
    =============================
    Ambient biome spawning. One job: make The Hollow's night-only identity real.

    THE CONSTRAINT THAT SHAPED THIS FILE
    ====================================
    spawning.xml supports time="Night", but it has NO gamestage gating - that
    lives only in gamestages.xml. So "only at night" and "enters at Cycle 5"
    cannot both come from ambient spawning. One of them has to give.

    Rather than drop either, the gate here is GEOGRAPHY instead of gamestage,
    which is the same idea the Field Notes already use: the wasteland and the
    burnt forest are late-game places, so putting The Hollow there at night
    gates it by where the player is willing to go rather than by a number.

    The result reads correctly at both ends of the game:

      * A day-3 player who walks into the wasteland after dark meets something
        silent that kills them. That is not unfair - the wasteland is supposed
        to do that, and it is the one biome where the game already says so.
      * From Cycle 5 The Hollow also enters the horde pools (entitygroups.xml),
        so it stops being a place you avoid and starts coming to you. That is
        the Turning doing its job.

    Deliberately NOT in the starter biomes. A silent stalker in the pine forest
    on night two is not a curfew, it is a rug-pull, and the mod's whole
    difficulty philosophy is that you should be able to name what killed you.

    Counts are low on purpose. The Hollow is an encounter, not a population.

    VERIFY-19 (docs/VERIFICATION.md): confirm the biome names below and the
    spawn attribute set against V3.2's Data/Config/spawning.xml.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- ==========================================================================
         WASTELAND - the harshest biome, and the one that already warns you
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/spawning/biome[@name='wasteland']">
        <spawn maxcount="2" respawndelay="2" time="Night" entitygroup="edNightPool" />
    </append>


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         BURNT FOREST - late-game adjacent, and thematically right for something
         that does not make a sound
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/spawning/biome[@name='burnt_forest']">
        <spawn maxcount="1" respawndelay="3" time="Night" entitygroup="edNightPool" />
    </append>

</configs>
